# ---- Game data. None of it belongs here, in any form. ----
#
# The blacklist below is deliberately wide. A Lindbergh game binary has no
# extension at all (lgj_final, vt3_final), so extensions alone never caught it
# and the one file this project exists to read was the one file git would have
# taken. Disc trees go by directory name as well, because a dropped-in tree
# brings shaders, audio banks and the ELF together.
*_final
disk0/
disk1/
*.iso
*.img
*.dat
*.elf
*.set
*.bin
*.afs
*.adx
*.aix
*.csb
*.xaf
*.pvr
*.dds

# Sega's shaders, both the source on the disc and cgc's 2005 output.
*.cg
*.asm_gl

# Shared objects lifted from a disc (libCg, libxerces-c, ...).
*.so
*.so.*

# What a run leaves behind: frame grabs and the cabinet's battery-backed store.
*.bmp
lindbergh_nvram.bin

# The disc's own config and launcher, if a tree is dropped in whole.
lgjrc
vt3rc
